qmx-panadapter patch: esp_hosted transport buffers -> PSRAM

Routes the esp_hosted WiFi transport DMA pool (per-packet TX/RX buffers)
into PSRAM instead of scarce internal DRAM. Without it the pool grows under
WiFi bursts, exhausts internal DMA RAM under QMX+FT8 load, and panics the
SDIO TX path (transport_drv_sta_tx -> assert(copy_buff)) -> reboot. Safe on
ESP32-P4: SOC_SDMMC_PSRAM_DMA_CAPABLE == 1, 1536-byte blocks are 64-byte
aligned. Target: managed_components (wiped by fullclean/dependency refresh -
re-apply after either). Pristine base: espressif/esp_hosted 1.4.0.

Apply from the repo root:  git apply tools/patches/esp_hosted_psram.patch

--- a/managed_components/espressif__esp_hosted/host/port/include/os_wrapper.h
+++ b/managed_components/espressif__esp_hosted/host/port/include/os_wrapper.h
@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@
 /* This is [malloc + aligned DMA] */
 #define MEM_ALLOC(x)       ({                                       \
 	esp_dma_mem_info_t dma_mem_info = {                             \
-		.extra_heap_caps = 0,                                       \
+		.extra_heap_caps = MALLOC_CAP_SPIRAM,                                       \
 		.dma_alignment_bytes = 64,                                  \
 	};                                                              \
 	void *tmp_buf = NULL;                                           \
